# The image is built from the repository root, because the frontend's build needs
# frontend/ as well as backend/ (#13). This file therefore governs that context:
# backend/.dockerignore is gone, and every rule it held lives here.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the build-context
# root: `__pycache__/` matches the root directory only and lets `app/__pycache__/`
# into the image, so every pattern above carries the `**/` prefix (`**/` also
# matches zero directories, so the root is covered).
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# The image's Python comes from its base image tag, not from a local pin, and the
# tests run outside the image.
**/.python-version
**/tests/

# Local data and secrets must never enter a build context.
**/uploads/
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store

# Context the build does not read: git's own history, the frontend's installed
# dependencies (the build stage runs `npm ci` itself) and the frontend's output
# (the build stage produces it).
**/.git/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
